From: OpenWrt WR11000 port
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: nsscc-qca8k: wait after releasing the chip reset

nss_cc_qca8k_clock_enable_and_reset() releases the QCA8084/QCA8386 reset
and registers the clocks immediately. When U-Boot has not brought the
chip up first (Cudy WR11000 booting from flash), the first access after
a cold start can find the critical branches still stuck at 'off', and
the whole clock controller fails to probe with -EBUSY. The vendor mdio
driver waits 100 ms after releasing the same reset; do the same.

---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-qca8k.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-qca8k.c
@@ -2180,6 +2180,12 @@
 	} else if (gpiod) {
 		msleep(100);
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(gpiod, 0);
+		/* Let the chip come out of reset before its clock
+		 * controller is programmed (the vendor driver waits
+		 * 100 ms here too). Without it a cold start can find
+		 * the critical branches still stuck at 'off'.
+		 */
+		msleep(100);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
